-- ============================================================
-- Weather renderer
-- Modes: "Rain" | "Snow" | "Thunder" | "Fireflies"
-- Features:
--   * Raycasted ground detection and per-frame collision for every drop/flake
--   * Per-drop variable fall speed and variable spawn height
--   * Circular splashes projected onto the impact surface (not a 2D overlay)
--   * Splashes are occlusion-tested so they no longer show through walls
--   * Snow uses the same raycasted collision system as rain
--   * Thunder mode: multiplied rain count, faster rain, jagged fading
--     thunderbolts with optional branches + screen flash
--   * Drops/flakes fall through invisible parts (Transparency >= 1)
--   * Behind-camera culling via WorldToScreen onScreen return value
--   * Random gusts that temporarily shift direction, speed and rain count
--   * Fireflies mode: wandering glowing dots with soft pulsing blink
--   * Intensity presets (Light / Medium / Heavy / Storm) applied via menu
--   * Configurable at runtime via the Matcha menu (UI.AddTab)
-- ============================================================

